<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Luke Kornet Paid $10.45m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Kornet is paid <strong>$10.45m</strong> because an undrafted player who lasts eight seasons on minimum deals eventually earns a mid-level contract from a club with one to spend.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted in 2017 and started on a two-way contract worth <strong>$75k</strong>.</li>
<li>He earned under <strong>$2.5m</strong> a season for seven straight years.</li>
<li>He signed two ten-day hardship contracts in the 2021-22 season alone.</li>
<li>San Antonio signed him in 2025 for <strong>$40.7m</strong> across four years.</li>
<li>His salary went from <strong>$2.09m</strong> to <strong>$11m</strong> in one summer.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has signed ten contracts across six clubs.</p>

